# Example for testing the "All Maximal U RAFs" algorithm.
#
# r0 is an uninhibited backbone reaction (food -> p), present in every uRAF.
# Two mutually-exclusive modules build on p:
#   Module A: rA1 (inhibited by b) produces a, then rA2 produces c
#   Module B: rB1 (inhibited by a) produces b
# a inhibits rB1 and b inhibits rA1, so a uRAF can use at most one module.
# rX is inhibited by the food element g, so it is always inhibited and never appears in a uRAF.
#
# There are 2 inhibiting elements to enumerate (a and b), so k = 2.
#
# Expected: two maximal uRAFs
#     {r0, rA1, rA2}   (module A, 3 reactions)
#     {r0, rB1}        (module B, 2 reactions)
# For comparison, the older single-shot "U RAF Algorithm" returns only {r0}.

Food: f, g

r0 : f [f] => p
rA1 : p [f] {b} => a
rA2 : a [f] => c
rB1 : p [f] {a} => b
rX : f [f] {g} => y
